    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d237">

                <pb facs="0298" n="290" sameAs="frus:frus1941v07/pg290"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">822.796/466: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Minister in Ecuador</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Long</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1941-10-03T18:00:00-05:00">October 3, 1941—6
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>286. Your 387, October 2, 10 p.m. We are delighted that the contract has been
                    signed. We hope that the Ecuadoran Government will now proceed without delay in
                    the cancellation of Sedta’s franchise, thus completing the elimination of
                        Sedta.<anchor n="75" xml:id="d237-f1"/> Please press this matter with the
                    Ecuadoran officials.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d237-f1" n="75" xml:id="d237-f1-content">
                <p>An Evaluating Committee was appointed to make a report to the Ecuadoran Minister
                    of Defense concerning the properties of Sedta; this was followed by
                    liquidation.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
